    "updated_at": "2025-05-26T06:04:42Z",
    "body": "Bump. libwebp which is included in every browser's source code supports lossless encoding out of the box and the files created are much smaller than PNGs. Only the flag needs to be passed. When calling canvas.toDataUrl / toBlob allowing passing an object with options that can be interpreted individually by every codec instead of a single float seems like a natural step forward",
